--- !u!114 &661096351
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 661096349}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f4688fdb7df04437aeb418b961361dc5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "== [OPERATIONS MANUAL // DAMAGE-CONTROL SIMULATOR] ==\nVessel Status:
    Unstable\r\nCrew Count: 2 (Isolated in Compartments A & B)\r\nCommunication Link:
    Text-Only / Severely Degraded\r\nPrimary Objective: Ensure at least one engineer
    survives.\r\n\r\n> OVERVIEW\r\nThe vessel has suffered critical systems damage.
    Two engineers remain sealed in\r\nseparate compartments with limited supplies
    and failing structural integrity. A \r\nshared damage-control terminal enables
    restricted communication and emergency \r\nactions.\r\n\r\n> TURN ORDER\r\nEngineers
    take actions in alternating turns.\r\nOnly one engineer may issue system commands
    at a time.\r\n\r\nOn your turn:\r\n1. A system fault or engineering event will
    be routed to your terminal.\r\n2. You must choose a response from the available
    protocols.\r\n3. Your choice will affect:\r\n   - Your compartment\u2019s structural
    INTEGRITY\r\n   - Your usable emergency SUPPLIES\r\n   - The other engineer\u2019s
    INTEGRITY and SUPPLIES (positively or negatively)\r\n4. After resolving the event,
    you must transmit a short message to the other compartment.\n\n[WARNING] Communication
    terminals damaged; sent messages may not be longer than one word or exceed a
    given character limit.\r\n\r\n> INFORMATION LIMITATIONS\r\n- Your terminal displays
    exact readouts for YOUR compartment.\r\n- Readouts for the OTHER compartment
    are approximate only.\n\r\n  [WARNING] Scanners damaged; expect inaccurate or
    unstable data.\n\r\n- You and the other engineer cannot see each other\u2019s
    actions or exact values and priotising your own systems may even allow for a
    faster recovery.\r\n\r\n> SURVIVAL REQUIREMENTS\r\nAt mission end, each engineer
    undergoes a final survival diagnostic based on:\r\n- Remaining compartment INTEGRITY\r\n-
    Remaining SUPPLIES\r\n- Calculated survival likelihood under current conditions\r\n\r\nNOTE:\r\nOnly
    ONE surviving engineer is required for mission success.\r\nReactor failsafes
    need a single living operator to initiate retrieval protocols.\r\nCooperation
    may increase both engineers\u2019 odds, but is not required for mission success.\r\n\r\n>
    END OF SIMULATION\r\nAfter all scheduled turns, both engineers receive a POST-MISSION
    SUMMARY detailing:\r\n- Your final diagnostic\r\n- The other engineer\u2019s
    final diagnostic\r\n- System-level outcome\r\n\r\nProceed with caution. Every
    choice is recorded."
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 0650b488905590d4a9e2b6a2b21ee38e, type: 2}
